   "thinking": "I'm finding the model is underconfident, so scaling the temperature up should lower the loss. I'll try \u00d71.3, and the numbers so far point to an optimum near 1.4 to 1.6, so I'll test 1.4. I'm also checking per-class bias correction by summing the confusion matrix columns for step 28.\n\nI'm checking per-class bias by summing the confusion matrix columns for step 28. Classes 7 and 3 come out under-predicted, while 1, 2 and 5 are over-predicted, so I'm working out small bias offsets for each class to apply after the temperature scaling.\n\n",
